## Context
Tracker 1252 (forge-less raid, gaze and merge). Design note conception/2026-10-27-git-notes-review-design.md
(author, drafted with ChatGPT) and the advisor ruling in 1252 (one refs/notes/review with a kind: field) left
five questions open that C3 (1273) and C4 (1274) depend on. The note orders a transport trial before migration;
the ruling waived it for 1252. Author ruling 2026-10-27: settle the design first, with transport trials.

## Questions to settle
1. Rebase survival: notes key on commit SHAs and raid rebases before every gate; notes.rewriteRef covers only
   local rebase/amend and must be configured in every environment. Carry, copy (git notes copy), or re-key?
2. Transport: notes refs are not fetched by default; concurrent appends from several hosts race on one ref;
   can each environment (doudou, padme, ChatGPT Work, Claude Code Web) fetch and push notes with its usual access?
   If not, the fallback (relay, dedicated branch) is chosen here.
3. The request's What as `git request-pull` output (note §2.1): kept, and where it lives.
4. Incremental review (note §4): links between rounds, delta vs full scope, findings that persist.
5. Identifiers (review_id, request_id, run_id, seat_id, gate_session_id) and the entry format; one ref vs four
   (the ruling's choice stands unless the trial or (1) overturns it).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Transport trial doudou <-> padme run and reported (publish, fetch, append, rebase, cleanup, recover; concurrent append).
- [ ] Web legs (ChatGPT Work, Claude Code Web) run by the author or recorded as not run.
- [ ] A design spec in conception/ answers questions 1-5, cites the trial, and is reviewed by a cross-family seat.
- [ ] The author accepts the spec; 1273, 1274 and 1276 are updated to it.

